            "paragraph": "Spatial monitoring is a remote sensing technology that provides \u201cthe eyes in the sky\" to supplement ground-based observations. Multispectral and hyperspectral sensors on satellites, drones, and aircraft are capable of detecting changes in crop health that are beyond the perception of the naked eye but are indicative of pest stress. The damage caused by insects such as aphids or leafhoppers results in changes in the light reflectance characteristics of the plant canopy. Remote sensing can map all these \u201cstress signatures\u201d across large fields to locate hotspots of infestation. This can be used to conduct specific scouting and intervention, as opposed to applying uniform treatment across the entire field. It is a technology that is particularly effective at tracking the geographic distribution of invasive species across large-scale landscapes [18].",
